\ Wrong twin (batch-h-wrong.lean's w_rintro_group): by-rintro[ x | y z ]
\ is Lean's rintro (x | y) z, two items, so each goal has z : b = a and
\ the goal b = a, with no binder left for by-intro: (Lean's introN
\ error). Read as one item, Lean's rintro (x | y z), the goals would keep
\ b = a -> b = a and the proof would go through.
theorem w_rintro_group
  Nat explicit: a  Nat explicit: b
  a b = b a = a a = ∧ ∨ explicit: h  b a = explicit: k
  b a =
:= by
  by-revert[ h k ]
  by-rintro[ x | y z ]
  by-intro: d
  ' d by-exact
  by-intro: d
  ' d by-exact
end w_rintro_group
